  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN containing **distinct** integers and an integer KKK (either 000 or 111).\n\nYour task is to find the total number of permutations of array AAA such that for **all** pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j)\nwith 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\leq i \\lt j \\leq N1≤i&lt;j≤N, and (i+j)(i + j)(i+j) being an **odd** number:\n\n\n(Ai+Aj)%2(A_i+A_j) \\% 2(Ai​+Aj​)%2 =K= K=K\nYou should output the count of such permutations modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK, as mentioned in statement.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the total number of permutations of array AAA satisfying the conditions, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "0≤K≤10 \\leq K \\leq 10≤K≤1",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1055\\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5 0\n6 10 1 4 8\n4 0\n17 13 21 3\n3 1\n1 2 3",
        "output": "0\n24\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: There is no permutation that satisfies the required conditions.\nTest Case 222: All the permutations of the array satisfy the required conditions.\nTest Case 333: Two permutations satisfy the conditions. They are:\n\n[1,2,3][1,2,3][1,2,3]: The pairs under consideration are (1,2)(1, 2)(1,2) and (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3). Here (A1+A2)%2=1=K(A_1+A_2) \\% 2 = 1 = K(A1​+A2​)%2=1=K. Similarly (A2+A3)%2=1=K(A_2+A_3) \\% 2 = 1 = K(A2​+A3​)%2=1=K.\n[3,2,1][3,2,1][3,2,1] The pairs under consideration are (1,2)(1, 2)(1,2) and (2,3)(2, 3)(2,3). Here (A1+A2)%2=1=K(A_1+A_2) \\% 2 = 1 = K(A1​+A2​)%2=1=K. Similarly (A2+A3)%2=1=K(A_2+A_3) \\% 2 = 1 = K(A2​+A3​)%2=1=K."
      }
    ]
  },
